---
mdv: "1.0"
title: NDJSON data
---

# Request latency by minute

One complete JSON value per line, which is the format's whole reason to
exist: a writer can append a record without rewriting a closing bracket,
and a reader can stop early. Blank lines are skipped, so a stream that was
flushed in batches still reads as one table.

`shed` appears from the second line on and is appended in first-seen
order, exactly as it would be in `json` — the two readers differ in how
records are framed and in nothing else.

```mdv line
title: p99 latency by minute
x: minute
y: p99
format: ndjson
---
{"minute": 1, "p99": 41.2}

{"minute": 2, "p99": 38.7, "shed": 4}
{"minute": 3, "p99": 52.9, "shed": 11}
```
